WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:07.120
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain a post apocalyptic drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:19.840
called “Carbon”. Watch out and take care!
The premise of the movie is set in the year 2067&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.040
when the earth has turned into a barren land&nbsp;
because of global warming. Oxygen and drinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.160
water are only available to the wealthy. Because&nbsp;
of the amount of carbon in the air, breathing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.680
out in the open is almost impossible. Houses and&nbsp;
buildings are supplied with partially clean air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.960
but outside them, people are required to&nbsp;
wear masks to stay alive. A healthy human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.120
will suffocate in about five minutes if they&nbsp;
do not wear a specialized oxygen mask. Oxygen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:53.440
which once used to be a basic part of nature, has&nbsp;
now turned into a product. Several million-dollar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.200
companies manufacture artificial oxygen in&nbsp;
bulk and sell it at an outrageous rate. 
&nbsp;

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.360
Since only the rich can afford it, the&nbsp;
government provides oxygen to the poor people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.440
at an affordable price. But such&nbsp;
oxygen is not of the best quality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:13.360
and can kill you with time. Most humans have&nbsp;
fled to Mars with gallons of oxygen and water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.600
as people on earth become more violent. Among all&nbsp;
kinds of oxygen, natural oxygen which can still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:26.240
be found in the Himalayas is the most in-demand.&nbsp;
It is sold for millions and is even rarer than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:35.040
diamonds. A few years ago people were so eager&nbsp;
to acquire oxygen, it caused several murders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.040
and protests. The government has since banned the&nbsp;
exploitation of natural oxygen strictly. Even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.600
rich aren’t allowed to trade or buy it. 
When the smuggling of such oxygen started,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.560
the government implemented a new rule according to&nbsp;
which people aren’t allowed to leave their houses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:57.280
after 6 pm. Anyone who is seen in a public place&nbsp;
during the curfew will be shot dead immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:03.440
The protagonist of the movie is a thirty-year-old&nbsp;
man named Random Shukla. He was born in Mumbai,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.120
India in the year 2037. Because of the condition&nbsp;
of the environment, he suffered from heart failure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.480
as soon as he took his first breath. Along with&nbsp;
him, forty-three percent of the infants born&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.200
that year suffered from heart failure. They have&nbsp;
been living with the help of an artificial heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.360
pacemaker until now. Random has to always carry&nbsp;
a bag with a device that is attached to his chest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.320
for the pacemaker to work. He claims that he&nbsp;
has only heard the stories of the green and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.600
blue earth and believes it is just a myth. 
The man cannot imagine a world where oxygen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:42.320
is abundant and water is not a luxury. His job&nbsp;
is to smuggle natural oxygen on a small scale.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.360
Because of the artificial heart, he is allowed&nbsp;
to carry two cans of oxygen everywhere he goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.160
which helps him smuggle it. At the beginning&nbsp;
of the movie, Random is woken up in his cell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.880
that he shares with several other workers. The&nbsp;
government announces that the supply of oxygen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:02.000
to houses will be stopped for a short period&nbsp;
of time in the morning. People are told to wear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.280
oxygen masks even when they are indoors during&nbsp;
that period. It is a regular day for Random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.200
until his associate calls him to a meeting with a client&nbsp;
named Yaqub who is willing to pay them millions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.560
to smuggle two cans of natural oxygen. 
On a normal day, someone from the client’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.720
side comes to pick up the oxygen but since&nbsp;
the security has been tighter these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.800
Random has to put his life in danger and go to the&nbsp;
client. He accepts the job instantly for money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.320
His ultimate goal is to collect enough money to&nbsp;
go to Mars and start a new life. Random and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.920
associate go to the ruins of a building to meet&nbsp;
Yaqub. He is a gangster and the biggest oxygen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:45.200
smuggler in Mumbai. The man has connections&nbsp;
all over Mars and supplies the rich with pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.800
Himalayan oxygen. Random tells him that he has a&nbsp;
license to carry natural oxygen so the job won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.920
be difficult for him. Yaqub’s men tear his clothes&nbsp;
to check if he is telling the truth. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.520
assured after seeing a blinking device attached&nbsp;
to his chest. The boss offers them ten million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:06.800
rupees each for the job but Random bargains they&nbsp;
should get at least forty million rupees. 
&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.480
Yaqub, who is still unsure of Random’s potential,&nbsp;
challenges him to a match of arm wrestling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:18.160
According to him, a smuggler needs courage more&nbsp;
than a license to close a deal. The match starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:24.000
during which, Yaqub takes off his oxygen mask&nbsp;
and makes Random do the same for a fair match.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.800
Soon, Random has trouble breathing and has to&nbsp;
deliberately lose to be able to wear the mask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:34.320
again. Because he showed courage, an impressed&nbsp;
Yaqub agrees to give him forty million. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.280
Random has to bring two cans of natural oxygen&nbsp;
to the other side of the checkpost and hand it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.760
to a client from Mars named Shah. He has to return&nbsp;
with the money before the evening curfew. If not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:51.680
the deal will be considered unsuccessful and&nbsp;
both Random and his associate will be killed. 
&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:57.040
In the following scene, Random is in the metro&nbsp;
station which is also the checkpoint. He holds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:03.360
cans of oxygen in his bag which, if checked, will&nbsp;
be exposed as illegal oxygen. Random is hoping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.640
that since he has a license, the security officer&nbsp;
wouldn’t go extra lengths to check the oxygen can.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.600
He is so nervous that he freezes when it is&nbsp;
his turn to go in. Just like he had predicted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.200
the officer doesn’t check the cans and lets him&nbsp;
go after scanning the license. He even advises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.720
Random to not lose his license or he can end up&nbsp;
in jail for the rest of his life. Sometime later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.600
he reaches an apartment where the client&nbsp;
Shah is waiting for him. Shah was flown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:34.800
Mars when he was only five years old by his&nbsp;
wealthy parents. He survives on high-quality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:40.480
artificial oxygen which is still not as good&nbsp;
as natural oxygen. Hence, the man is always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.760
keen on buying cans of natural oxygen. 
He has recently returned to earth for the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:51.440
reason. Random notices a glass full of water&nbsp;
on the table. He cannot help but stare at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.480
strange sight of clean water which is usually&nbsp;
reserved for wealthy people. Shah offers it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.960
him which surprises Random. He doesn’t accept&nbsp;
the glass and gets straight to the business instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.040
Shah claims that residents of Mars only&nbsp;
return to earth for pleasure or for business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:12.160
he is there for the former. Random gets the&nbsp;
hint and brings out the cans of fresh oxygen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.800
The oxygen was collected and packaged at&nbsp;
eight hundred meters above sea level, making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:22.960
it non-toxic and a hundred percent pure. 
Shah inspects the cans and appears to be impressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:28.720
by them. Yet, when Random asks for the payment,&nbsp;
he hesitates. The oxygen might have moisture mixed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.960
in it which means he cannot pay without testing&nbsp;
it first. Random replies that even if the oxygen has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:40.080
moisture, it is the last batch coming from the&nbsp;
Himalayas. Soon, these kinds will also not be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.120
available for purchase. He suggests the client&nbsp;
use the opportunity wisely but his words make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.720
Shah suspect him even more. As the two get into a&nbsp;
heated conversation, Shah mentions that the earth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:56.640
is about to shake violently very soon. Just as&nbsp;
he says that the coffee table starts shaking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.800
Random notices that the table is actually a box&nbsp;
that has something or someone inside of it. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.680
two do not acknowledge the shaking and continue&nbsp;
the bargain. They do not go on for long before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:13.280
the box moves again. Random had come to end the&nbsp;
deal without violence but seeing that the client&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:19.600
doesn’t want to pay, he brings out a gun. However,&nbsp;
Shah is not someone who backs up. He, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:25.440
points a gun at Random. While Random is nervous,&nbsp;
Shah appears to be excited. He claims that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:30.240
life on Mars was boring and their conversation&nbsp;
is giving him an adrenaline rush.  
&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.520
In split seconds, Random shoots the man on the&nbsp;
forehead and kills him. He had realized that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:41.280
only one of them could walk away alive, so he took&nbsp;
the only opportunity that he had. Following that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.920
he opens the box that had been moving&nbsp;
and is surprised to see a girl inside of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:51.200
She is tied up and gagged and seems to have been&nbsp;
kidnapped. Unsure what she is capable of doing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:57.200
he points his gun at her as well. The girl freezes&nbsp;
in shock but is relieved when he frees her hands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:03.040
Random threatens her to stay low and keep quiet&nbsp;
because he doesn’t want to have to kill her. As they talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.800
the girl reveals that the man who Random just&nbsp;
killed is not Shah. The real Shah’s dead body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.680
lies in the bedroom. It turns out that the man&nbsp;
Random was talking untill now was pretending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:19.920
to be Shah to stall him. He was actually a hitman&nbsp;
who had killed Shah moments before. The girl also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:25.440
reveals that the hitman was about to smuggle her&nbsp;
to Mars before Random arrived. Random knows that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.640
he returns to Yaqub without the money, he will&nbsp;
end up dead. Hence, he looks around the house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:35.920
and finds several gallons of clean water. He&nbsp;
almost doesn’t believe the treasure before him. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:40.640
wants to smuggle them out but the containers have&nbsp;
an in-built security system which means if someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.360
tries to take them out of the building without&nbsp;
a passcode, the police will be alerted. 
&nbsp;

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.200
Right then, it is announced that the&nbsp;
evening curfew has been implemented.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.640
Random’s deal has failed, so he is bound to be&nbsp;
killed if he returns home. He has to quickly think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.640 --> 00:09:00.560
of a way to run away from the city before Yaqub&nbsp;
finds him. Somewhere else, Yaqub is impatiently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.200
waiting for his arrival. When he is notified that&nbsp;
the curfew is in action, he takes off Random’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:10.720
friend’s oxygen mask and eventually kills the&nbsp;
man by suffocating him. Back in the apartment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:16.400
Random asks the girl about her true identity. She&nbsp;
introduces herself as Pari and claims that she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:22.240
a refugee who was bought by Shah. He planned to&nbsp;
take her to Mars as his mistress. But as soon as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:28.560
she arrived there, the hitman killed Shah and held&nbsp;
her hostage. As the two talk, Random’s artificial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:33.760
heart alerts him of overheating. Pari realizes&nbsp;
that she is making him nervous which makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:39.280
blush even more. When asked what she wants to do&nbsp;
now, Pari claims that she will travel the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:45.440
Weirdly enough, she keeps repeating the same thing&nbsp;
as her voice turns more and more robotic. Random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.640
asks her if she is fine and soon realizes that&nbsp;
she is just a robot who has been programmed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:59.120
think she is a human. Pari malfunctions and turns&nbsp;
her power off and Random is left all alone. 
&nbsp;

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.920
He plans to run away as soon as the curfew&nbsp;
is lifted. A few hours later, he breathes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:08.720
in the exclusive oxygen out of curiosity. It&nbsp;
doesn’t go well because the whiff of clean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:14.080
oxygen makes him pass out. When he wakes up the&nbsp;
next morning, Yaqub and his people are standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.640
in front of him. They tie him to a chair,&nbsp;
assuming that he killed Shah for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:23.920
gallons of water. Random tries to explain what&nbsp;
actually happened but Yaqub doesn’t believe him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.880
His men do not notice the security system&nbsp;
attached to the water containers and start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.920
to carry them to the elevator. Yaqub leaves&nbsp;
Random tied to a chair so he would be arrested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:39.920
for killing Shah and the hitman. However, as they&nbsp;
try to walk away with the water, an alarm rings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:47.280
alerting the police. Just then, Pari switches on&nbsp;
and unties Random’s hands. The police catch Yaqub&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.040
and his gang. Since they only care about&nbsp;
the gallons of water being smuggled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:56.640
they do not bother to search for Random and&nbsp;
Pari. In the end, the pair manages to escape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:00.560
through a secret passage.  
